tions in the free-response booklet. Use a pencil or pen with black or dark blue ink. You may use the available paper for scratch work, but credit will only be given for responses that are written in the free-response booklet.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThe inclusion of source material in this exam is not intended as an endorsement by College Board of the content, ideas, or values expressed in the material. The sources that appear in the AP Microeconomics Exam represent a range of graphs, charts, and data, as appropriate for measuring the college-level knowledge and skills that are the focus of this course. AP students are not expected or asked to subscribe to any specific cultural, political, or socioeconomic values, but they are expected to analyze perspectives that may be different from their own and to analyze data principles that apply to the functions of individual economic decision-makers.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThere may be references in AP testing materials to companies, products, and brands that are owned by others and subject to trademark law. Neither College Board nor the AP testing materials are affiliated with or endorsed by these trademark owners.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-06-25T17:06:37-04:00\\u0022\\u003E1782421597\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"2486\",\"internal_id\":\"overview-ap-macro-linear-multiday-part2\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Day 2 Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EDay 2 of the AP Macroeconomics Exam consists of the multiple-choice section.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003EMultiple Choice\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThe multiple-choice section has 60 questions and lasts 1 hour and 10 minutes. This section represents 66.67% of your total score. Your score on the multiple-choice section is based on the number of questions answered correctly. Points are not deducted for incorrect answers or unanswered questions.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ETaking the Exam\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EYou can go back and forth between questions in the section until time expires. The clock will turn red when 5 minutes remain\\u2014\\u003Cem\\u003Ethe proctor will not give you any time updates or warnings\\u003C\\/em\\u003E. Once time expires in the section, you cannot return to it.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EA calculator is available in this application and can be accessed throughout the exam.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EYou may use scratch paper for notes and planning, but credit will only be given for responses entered in this application. When time expires in the section, all answers you have already entered will be submitted.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThe inclusion of source material in this exam is not intended as an endorsement by College Board of the content, ideas, or values expressed in the material. The sources that appear in the AP Macroeconomics Exam represent a range of graphs, charts, and data, as appropriate for measuring the college-level knowledge and skills that are the focus of this course. AP students are not expected or asked to subscribe to any specific cultural, political, or socioeconomic values, but they are expected to analyze perspectives that may be different from their own and to analyze data to understand macroeconomic measurements, models, and policies.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThere may be references in AP testing materials to companies, products, and brands that are owned by others and subject to trademark law. Neither College Board nor the AP testing materials are affiliated with or endorsed by these trademark owners.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-06-25T17:06:37-04:00\\u0022\\u003E1782421597\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"2466\",\"internal_id\":\"overview-ap-macro-linear-multiday-part1\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Day 1 Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EDay 1 of the AP Macroeconomics Exam consists of the free-response section.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003EFree Response\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThe free-response section has 3 questions and lasts 1 hour. This section represents 33.33% of your total score. Question 1 is a long free-response question, worth 10 points. Questions 2 and 3 are short free-response questions, each worth 5 points.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ETaking the Exam\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EYou can go back and forth between questions in the section until time expires. The clock will turn red when 5 minutes remain\\u2014\\u003Cem\\u003Ethe proctor will not give you any time updates or warnings\\u003C\\/em\\u003E. Once time expires in the section, you cannot return to it.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EA calculator is available in this application and can be accessed throughout the exam.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThe free-response questions are in this application, but you must write your responses to the questions in the free-response booklet. Use a pencil or pen with black or dark blue ink. You may use the available paper for scratch work, but credit will only be given for responses that are written in the free-response booklet.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThe inclusion of source material in this exam is not intended as an endorsement by College Board of the content, ideas, or values expressed in the material. The sources that appear in the AP Macroeconomics Exam represent a range of graphs, charts, and data, as appropriate for measuring the college-level knowledge and skills that are the focus of this course. AP students are not expected or asked to subscribe to any specific cultural, political, or socioeconomic values, but they are expected to analyze perspectives that may be different from their own and to analyze data to understand macroeconomic measurements, models, and policies.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThere may be references in AP testing materials to companies, products, and brands that are owned by others and subject to trademark law. Neither College Board nor the AP testing materials are affiliated with or endorsed by these trademark owners.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-06-25T17:06:37-04:00\\u0022\\u003E1782421597\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"2456\",\"internal_id\":\"overview-ap-macro-linear-singleday\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThe AP Macroeconomics Exam has 2 sections and lasts 2 hours and 10 minutes.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ESection I: Multiple Choice\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThe multiple-choice section has 60 questions and lasts 1 hour and 10 minutes. This section represents 66.67% of your total score. Your score on the multiple-choice section is based on the number of questions answered correctly. Points are not deducted for incorrect answers or unanswered questions.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ESection II: Free Response\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThe free-response section has 3 questions and lasts 1 hour. This section represents 33.33% of your total score. Question 1 is a long free-response question, worth 10 points. Questions 2 and 3 are short free-response questions, each worth 5 points.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ETaking the Exam\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EEach section is timed separately. You can go back and forth between questions in a section until time expires. The clock will turn red when 5 minutes remain in the section\\u2014\\u003Cem\\u003Ethe proctor will not give you any time updates or warnings\\u003C\\/em\\u003E. You cannot move ahead to a different section. Once time expires in a section, you cannot return to it.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EA calculator is available in this application and can be accessed throughout the exam.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EYou may use the available paper for scratch work, but credit for Section I: Multiple Choice will only be given for responses entered in this application. When time expires in a section, all answers you have already entered will be submitted.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EFor Section II: Free Response, the questions are in this application, but you must write your responses to the questions in the free-response booklet. Use a pencil or pen with black or dark blue ink. You may use the available paper for scratch work, but credit will only be given for responses that are written in the free-response booklet.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThe inclusion of source material in this exam is not intended as an endorsement by College Board of the content, ideas, or values expressed in the material. The sources that appear in the AP Macroeconomics Exam represent a range of graphs, charts, and data, as appropriate for measuring the college-level knowledge and skills that are the focus of this course. AP students are not expected or asked to subscribe to any specific cultural, political, or socioeconomic values, but they are expected to analyze perspectives that may be different from their own and to analyze data to understand macroeconomic measurements, models, and policies.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThere may be references in AP testing materials to companies, products, and brands that are owned by others and subject to trademark law. Neither College Board nor the AP testing materials are affiliated with or endorsed by these trademark owners.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-06-25T17:06:37-04:00\\u0022\\u003E1782421597\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"2476\",\"internal_id\":\"overview-ap-calc-bc-linear-multiday-part2\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Day 2 Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EDay 2 of the AP Calculus BC Exam consists of the multiple-choice section.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003EMultiple Choice\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThe multiple-choice section has 2 parts and represents 50% of your total score. Your score on the multiple-choice section is based on the number of questions answered correctly. Points are not deducted for incorrect answers or unanswered questions.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch3\\u003EMultiple Choice, Part A\\u003C\\/h3\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EPart A of the multiple-choice section has 30 questions and lasts 1 hour. \\u003Cem\\u003EA calculator is not allowed for this part of the exam.\\u003C\\/em\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch3\\u003EMultiple Choice, Part B\\u003C\\/h3\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EPart B of the multiple-choice section has 15 questions and lasts 45 minutes. \\u003Cem\\u003EA graphing calculator is required for some questions on this part of the exam.\\u003C\\/em\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ETaking the Exam\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EEach part is timed separately. You can go back and forth between questions in a part until time expires. The clock will turn red when 5 minutes remain in the part\\u2014\\u003Cem\\u003Ethe proctor will not give you any time updates or warnings\\u003C\\/em\\u003E. You cannot move ahead to a different part. Once time expires in a part, you cannot return to it.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EQuestions in Part B require the use of a calculator. You may use a handheld graphing calculator or the calculator available in this application.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EYou may use the available paper for scratch work, but credit will only be given for responses entered in this application. When time expires in a part, all answers you have already entered will be submitted.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThere may be references in AP testing materials to companies, products, and brands that are owned by others and subject to trademark law. Neither College Board nor the AP testing materials are affiliated with or endorsed by these trademark owners.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-06-25T17:06:37-04:00\\u0022\\u003E1782421597\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"2441\",\"internal_id\":\"overview-ap-calc-bc-linear-multiday-part1\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Day 1 Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EDay 1 of the AP Calculus BC Exam consists of the free-response section.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003EFree Response\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThe free-response section has 2 parts and represents 50% of your total score. There are 6 questions in this section, and each of the questions counts equally toward your score.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch3\\u003EFree Response, Part A\\u003C\\/h3\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EPart A of the free-response section has 2 questions and lasts 30 minutes. \\u003Cem\\u003EA graphing calculator is required for the questions on this part of the exam.\\u003C\\/em\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch3\\u003EFree Response, Part B\\u003C\\/h3\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EPart B of the free-response section has 4 questions and lasts 1 hour.\\u003Cem\\u003E A calculator is not allowed for this part of the exam.\\u003C\\/em\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ETaking the Exam\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EEach part is timed separately. You can go back and forth between questions in a part until time expires. The clock will turn red when 5 minutes remain in the part\\u2014\\u003Cem\\u003Ethe proctor will not give you any time updates or warnings\\u003C\\/em\\u003E. You cannot move ahead to a different part. Once time expires in a part, you cannot return to it.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EQuestions in Part A require the use of a calculator. You may use a handheld graphing calculator or the calculator available in this application.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThe free-response questions are in this application, but you must write your responses to the questions in the free-response booklet. Use a pencil or pen with black or dark blue ink. You may use the available paper for scratch work, but credit will only be given for responses that are written in the free-response booklet.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThere may be references in AP testing materials to companies, products, and brands that are owned by others and subject to trademark law. Neither College Board nor the AP testing materials are affiliated with or endorsed by these trademark owners.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-06-25T17:06:37-04:00\\u0022\\u003E1782421597\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"2461\",\"internal_id\":\"overview-ap-calc-bc-linear-singleday\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EThe AP Calculus BC Exam has 2 sections and lasts 3 hours and 15 minutes.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ESection I: Multiple Choice\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThe multiple-choice section has 2 parts and represents 50% of your total score. Your score on the multiple-choice section is based on the number of questions answered correctly. Points are not deducted for incorrect answers or unanswered questions.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch3\\u003ESection I, Part A: Multiple Choice\\u003C\\/h3\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EPart A of the multiple-choice section has 30 questions and lasts 1 hour. \\u003Cem\\u003EA calculator is not allowed for this part of the exam.\\u003C\\/em\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch3\\u003ESection I, Part B: Multiple Choice\\u003C\\/h3\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EPart B of the multiple-choice section has 15 questions and lasts 45 minutes. \\u003Cem\\u003EA graphing calculator is required for some questions on this part of the exam.\\u003C\\/em\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ESection II: Free Response\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThe free-response section has 2 parts and represents 50% of your total score. There are 6 questions in this section, and each of the questions counts equally toward your score.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch3\\u003ESection II, Part A: Free Response\\u003C\\/h3\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EPart A of the free-response section has 2 questions and lasts 30 minutes. \\u003Cem\\u003EA graphing calculator is required for the questions on this part of the exam.\\u003C\\/em\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch3\\u003ESection II, Part B: Free Response\\u003C\\/h3\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EPart B of the free-response section has 4 questions and lasts 1 hour. \\u003Cem\\u003EA calculator is not allowed for this part of the exam.\\u003C\\/em\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ETaking the Exam\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EEach section and part is timed separately. You can go back and forth between questions in a part until time expires. The clock will turn red when 5 minutes remain in the part\\u2014\\u003Cem\\u003Ethe proctor will not give you any time updates or warnings\\u003C\\/em\\u003E. You cannot move ahead to a different part. Once time expires in a section or part, you cannot return to it.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EQuestions in Section I, Part B and Section II, Part A require the use of a calculator. You may use a handheld graphing calculator or the calculator available in this application.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EYou may use the available paper for scratch work, but credit for Section I: Multiple Choice will only be given for responses entered in this application. When time expires in a section or part, all answers you have already entered will be submitted.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EFor Section II: Free Response, the questions are in this application, but you must write your responses to the questions in the free-response booklet. Use a pencil or pen with black or dark blue ink. You may use the available paper for scratch work, but credit will only be given for responses that are written in the free-response booklet.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThere may be references in AP testing materials to companies, products, and brands that are owned by others and subject to trademark law. Neither College Board nor the AP testing materials are affiliated with or endorsed by these trademark owners.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":