tRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN\\u0022\\u003ENeither \\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun Highlight SCXW65334460 BCX0 NormalTextRun ContextualSpellingAndGrammarErrorV2Themed\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN\\u0022\\u003ECollege\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun Highlight SCXW65334460 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN\\u0022\\u003E Board nor the AP testing materials are affiliated with or endorsed by these trademark owners.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW65334460 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-01-06T11:11:18-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1767715878\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1956\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-confirm-tts\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Confirm Your Text-to-Speech Voices\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EOpen \\u003Cstrong\\u003ESettings \\u003C\\/strong\\u003Eon the text-to-speech player to choose the voices you want to hear during the exam. Then listen to the following passages.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\",\"id\":\"checkin-confirm-tts-p1\"},{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESample English Passage\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EHello! This is a short paragraph to test your text-to-speech voice. You should hear clear pronunciation, even pacing, and a natural tone. If you do not like the way this voice sounds, please select another one.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\",\"id\":\"checkin-confirm-tts-en\"},{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESample Spanish Passage\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp lang=\\u0022es\\u0022\\u003E\\u00a1Hola! Este es un breve p\\u00e1rrafo para probar la herramienta texto a voz. Deber\\u00edas escuchar una pronunciaci\\u00f3n clara, un ritmo uniforme y un tono natural. Si no te gusta la voz, por favor elige otra.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\",\"id\":\"checkin-confirm-tts-es\"},{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESample Chinese Passage\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp lang=\\u0022zh\\u0022\\u003E\\u4f60\\u597d\\uff01\\u8fd9\\u662f\\u4e00\\u4e2a\\u7528\\u4e8e\\u6d4b\\u8bd5\\u6587\\u672c\\u8f6c\\u8bed\\u97f3\\u7684\\u7b80\\u77ed\\u6bb5\\u843d\\u3002\\u4f60\\u5e94\\u8be5\\u542c\\u5230\\u6e05\\u6670\\u7684\\u53d1\\u97f3\\u3001\\u5747\\u5300\\u7684\\u8bed\\u901f\\u548c\\u81ea\\u7136\\u7684\\u8bed\\u8c03\\u3002\\u5982\\u679c\\u6709\\u4e9b\\u8bcd\\u542c\\u8d77\\u6765\\u751f\\u786c\\u3001\\u592a\\u5feb\\u6216\\u50cf\\u673a\\u5668\\u4eba\\uff0c\\u8bf7\\u8c03\\u6574\\u8bbe\\u7f6e\\u6216\\u5c1d\\u8bd5\\u5176\\u4ed6\\u8bed\\u97f3\\uff0c\\u76f4\\u5230\\u58f0\\u97f3\\u542c\\u8d77\\u6765\\u81ea\\u7136\\u6d41\\u7545\\u3002\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\",\"id\":\"checkin-confirm-tts-zh\"},{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESample German Passage\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp lang=\\u0022de\\u0022\\u003EHallo! Dies ist ein kurzer Absatz, um deine Text-zu-Sprache-Stimme zu testen. Du solltest eine klare Aussprache, gleichm\\u00e4\\u00dfiges Tempo und einen nat\\u00fcrlichen Klang h\\u00f6ren. Wenn einige W\\u00f6rter hart, zu schnell oder k\\u00fcnstlich klingen, passe die Einstellungen an oder w\\u00e4hle eine andere Stimme.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\",\"id\":\"checkin-confirm-tts-de\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-01-06T11:19:05-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1767716345\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1936\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-ap-networking-day2\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Day 2 Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EDay 2 of the AP Networking Exam consists of a multiple-choice section.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003EMultiple Choice\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThis section has 36 questions and lasts 1 hour. This section represents 50% of your total score. Your score on this section is based on the number of questions answered correctly. Points are not deducted for incorrect answers or unanswered questions.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ETaking the Exam\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EYou can go back and forth between questions in the section until time expires. The clock will turn red when 5 minutes remain\\u2014\\u003Cem\\u003Ethe proctor will not give you any time updates or warnings\\u003C\\/em\\u003E. Once time expires in the section, you cannot return to it.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EA calculator is available in this application and can be accessed throughout the exam.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EYou may use scratch paper for notes and planning, but credit will only be given for responses entered in this application. Any text you enter as an annotation will \\u003Cem\\u003Enot\\u003C\\/em\\u003E be included in your answer submissions. When time expires in the section, all answers you have already entered will be submitted.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThere may be references in AP testing materials to companies, products, and brands that are owned by others and subject to trademark law. Neither College Board nor the AP testing materials are affiliated with or endorsed by these trademark owners.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-02-11T11:37:04-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1770827824\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1946\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-ap-networking-day1\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Day 1 Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EDay 1 of the AP Networking Exam consists of a multiple-choice section.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003EMultiple Choice\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThis section has 36 questions and lasts 1 hour. This section represents 50% of your total score. Your score on this section is based on the number of questions answered correctly. Points are not deducted for incorrect answers or unanswered questions.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ETaking the Exam\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EYou can go back and forth between questions in the section until time expires. The clock will turn red when 5 minutes remain\\u2014\\u003Cem\\u003Ethe proctor will not give you any time updates or warnings\\u003C\\/em\\u003E. Once time expires in the section, you cannot return to it.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EA calculator is available in this application and can be accessed throughout the exam.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EYou may use scratch paper for notes and planning, but credit will only be given for responses entered in this application. Any text you enter as an annotation will \\u003Cem\\u003Enot\\u003C\\/em\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003E \\u003C\\/strong\\u003Ebe included in your answer submissions. When time expires in the section, all answers you have already entered will be submitted.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThere may be references in AP testing materials to companies, products, and brands that are owned by others and subject to trademark law. Neither College Board nor the AP testing materials are affiliated with or endorsed by these trademark owners.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-02-11T11:36:37-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1770827797\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1971\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-ap-networking\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EThe AP Networking Exam has 2 multiple-choice sections and lasts 2 hours.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ESection I: Multiple Choice\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThe first multiple-choice section has 36 questions and lasts 1 hour. This section represents 50% of your total score. Your score on this section is based on the number of questions answered correctly. Points are not deducted for incorrect answers or unanswered questions.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ESection II: Multiple Choice\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThe second multiple-choice section has 36 questions and lasts 1 hour. This section represents 50% of your total score. Your score on this section is based on the number of questions answered correctly. Points are not deducted for incorrect answers or unanswered questions.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ETaking the Exam\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EEach section is timed separately. You can go back and forth between questions in a section until time expires. The clock will turn red when 5 minutes remain in the section\\u2014\\u003Cem\\u003Ethe proctor will not give you any time updates or warnings\\u003C\\/em\\u003E. You cannot move ahead to a different section. Once time expires in a section, you cannot return to it.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EA calculator is available in this application and can be accessed throughout the exam.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EYou may use scratch paper for notes and planning, but credit will only be given for responses entered in this application. Any text you enter as an annotation will \\u003Cem\\u003Enot\\u003C\\/em\\u003E be included in your answer submissions. When time expires in a section, all answers you have already entered will be submitted.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThere may be references in AP testing materials to companies, products, and brands that are owned by others and subject to trademark law. Neither College Board nor the AP testing materials are affiliated with or endorsed by these trademark owners.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-02-11T11:36:01-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1770827761\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1896\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-ap-music-theory-singleday-part2\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThe AP Music Theory Exam has 2 sections and lasts approximately 2 hours and 35 minutes.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESection I: Multiple Choice\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThe multiple-choice section of the AP Music Theory Exam includes 2 parts and lasts approximately 1 hour and 20 minutes. There are 75 multiple-choice questions in Section I.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch3\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESection I, Part A\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/h3\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThis part of the exam lasts approximately 45 minutes and includes multiple-choice questions that are based on audio recordings.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch3\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESection I, Part B\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/h3\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThis part of the exam lasts approximately 35 minutes and includes multiple-choice questions that are based on written concepts and musical scores.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESection II: Free Response\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThe free-response section of the AP Music Theory Exam includes 9 free-response questions and lasts approximately 1 hour and 15 minutes.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch3\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESection II, Part A\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/h3\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThis part of the exam includes 7 free-response questions and lasts approximately 1 hour and 10 minutes. All questions require written responses which you will write in the separate free-response booklet. Questions 1 through 4 in this part include audio recordings.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch3\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESection II, Part B\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/h3\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThis part of the exam includes 2 sight-singing questions and lasts approximately 5 minutes. You will record your responses to the questions in this application.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThe inclusion of source material in this exam is not intended as an endorsement by College Board of the content, ideas, or values expressed in the material. The sources that appear in the AP Music Theory Exam represent a range of different works, as appropriate for measuring the college-level knowledge and skills that are the focus of this course. AP students are not expected or asked to subscribe to any specific cultural or political values, but they are expected to analyze and interpret sources in their disciplinary contexts.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThere may be references in AP testing materials to companies, products, and brands that are owned by others and subject to trademark law. Neither College Board nor the AP testing materials are affiliated with or endorsed by these trademark owners.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-07-10T17:31:11-04:00\\u0022\\u003E1783719071\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1916\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-ap-cybersecurity\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThe AP\\u0026nbsp;Cybersecurity\\u0026nbsp;Exam has 2 sections and lasts\\u0026nbsp;2\\u0026nbsp;hours.\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ESection I: Multiple Choice\\u0026nbsp;\\u003Cstrong\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThe multiple-choice section has\\u0026nbsp;60 questions and lasts 1 hour\\u0026nbsp;and 20 minutes. This section\\u0026nbsp;represents\\u0026nbsp;66% of your total score. Your score on the multiple-choice section is based on the number of questions answered correctly. Points are not deducted for incorrect answers or unanswered questions.\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ESection II: Free Response\\u0026nbsp;\\u003Cstrong\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThe free-response section has\\u0026nbsp;2\\u0026nbsp;questions and lasts\\u0026nbsp;40 minutes. This section\\u0026nbsp;represents\\u0026nbsp;34% of your total score.\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ETaking the Exam\\u0026nbsp; \\u003Cstrong\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EEach section is timed separately. You can go back and forth between questions in a section until time expires. The clock will turn red when 5 minutes\\u0026nbsp;remain\\u0026nbsp;in the section\\u2014\\u003Cem\\u003Ethe proctor will not give you any\\u0026nbsp;time\\u0026nbsp;updates or warnings\\u003C\\/em\\u003E. You cannot move ahead to a different section. Once time expires in a section, you cannot\\u0026nbsp;return to\\u0026nbsp;it.\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EYou may use scratch paper for notes and planning, but credit will only be\\u0026nbsp;given for\\u0026nbsp;responses entered in this application. Any text you enter as an annotation will\\u003Cem\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;not\\u003C\\/em\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;be included in your answer submissions. When time expires in a section, all answers you have already entered will be\\u0026nbsp;submitted.\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThere may be references in AP testing materials to companies, products, and brands that are owned by others and subject to trademark law.\\u202fNeither\\u0026nbsp;College\\u0026nbsp;Board nor the AP testing materials are affiliated with or endorsed by these trademark owners.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-01-06T11:13:43-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1767716023\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1911\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-ap-music-theory-singleday-part1\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThe AP Music Theory Exam has 2 sections and lasts approximately 2 hours and 35 minutes.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESection I: Multiple Choice\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThe multiple-choice section of the AP Music Theory Exam includes 2 parts and lasts approximately 1 hour and 20 minutes. There are 75 multiple-choice questions in Section I.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch3\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESection I, Part A\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/h3\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThis part of the exam lasts approximately 45 minutes and includes multiple-choice questions that are based on audio recordings.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch3\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESection I, Part B\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/h3\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThis part of the exam lasts approximately 35 minutes and includes multiple-choice questions that are based on written concepts and musical scores.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESection II: Free Response\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThe free-response section of the AP Music Theory Exam includes 9 free-response questions and lasts approximately 1 hour and 15 minutes.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch3\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESection II, Part A\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/h3\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThis part of the exam includes 7 free-response questions and lasts approximately 1 hour and 10 minutes. All questions require written responses which you will write in the separate free-response booklet. Questions 1 through 4 in this part include audio recordings.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch3\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESection II, Part B\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/h3\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThis part of the exam includes 2 sight-singing questions and lasts approximately 5 minutes. You will record your responses to the questions in this application.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThe inclusion of source material in this exam is not intended as an endorsement by College Board of the content, ideas, or values expressed in the material. The sources that appear in the AP Music Theory Exam represent a range of different works, as appropriate for measuring the college-level knowledge and skills that are the focus of this course. AP students are not expected or asked to subscribe to any specific cultural or political values, but they are expected to analyze and interpret sources in their disciplinary contexts.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThere may be references in AP testing materials to companies, products, and brands that are owned by others and subject to trademark law. Neither College Board nor the AP testing materials are affiliated with or endorsed by these trademark owners.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-07-10T17:29:05-04:00\\u0022\\u003E1783718945\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"2001\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-ap-japanese-day2\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Day 2 Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EContent is TK\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-01-06T11:19:55-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1767716395\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1996\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-ap-japanese-day1\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Day 1 Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EContent is TK\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-01-06T11:19:55-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1767716395\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1986\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-ap-japanese\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"inte