e\":\"Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EContent is TK\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-01-06T11:20:37-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1767716437\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"2021\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-ap-french-day2\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Day 2 Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EContent is TK\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-01-06T11:20:37-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1767716437\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"2061\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-ap-french-day1\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Day 1 Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EContent is TK\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-01-06T11:21:29-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1767716489\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"2016\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-ap-french\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EContent is TK\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-01-06T11:20:37-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1767716437\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"2056\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-ap-spanish-lang-day2\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Day 2 Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EContent is TK\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-01-06T11:21:29-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1767716489\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"2066\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-ap-spanish-lang-day1\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Day 1 Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EContent is TK\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-01-06T11:21:29-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1767716489\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"2076\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-ap-music-theory-day2\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Day 2 Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EContent is TK\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-01-06T11:21:29-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1767716489\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"2071\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-ap-music-theory-multiday-part1\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Day 1 Overview: Free Response\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThe free-response section of the AP Music Theory Exam includes 3 free-response questions and lasts approximately 23 minutes. All 3 questions require written responses. Questions 1 and 2 include audio sources, and there is a one-minute break before proceeding to question 3. The free-response questions are referenced in this application, but you will write your responses to the questions in the separate free-response booklet.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003ESource materials may have been edited for the purpose of this pilot exam.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThe inclusion of source material in this pilot exam is not intended as an endorsement by College Board of the content, ideas, or values expressed in the material. The sources that appear in the AP Music Theory Exam represent a range of different works, as appropriate for measuring the college-level knowledge and skills that are the focus of this course. AP students are not expected or asked to subscribe to any specific cultural or political values, but they are expected to analyze and interpret sources in their disciplinary contexts.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThere may be references in AP testing materials to companies, products, and brands that are owned by others and subject to trademark law. Neither College Board nor the AP testing materials are affiliated with or endorsed by these trademark owners.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-03-24T10:12:05-04:00\\u0022\\u003E1774361525\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1906\",\"internal_id\":\"sat-wkd-overview-video-transcript\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Get Ready for the Digital SAT\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW241311215 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EIf you\\u2019re taking the test on a weekend, here\\u2019s how it\\u2019ll work.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW241311215 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EBefore test day, head to the Practice and Prepare section of the Bluebook homepage and start practicing.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW241311215 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EYou can explore the tools and features of the app and try a few sample questions in the test preview or take a full-length practice test.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW241311215 BCX0 NormalTextRun CommentStart CommentHighlightPipeRest CommentHighlightRest\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EThe week of the test, \\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW241311215 BCX0 NormalTextRun CommentHighlightRest\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003Eyou\\u0027ll complete a quick exam setup to check your device and get your admission ticket.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP CommentHighlightPipeRest SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW241311215 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EYou\\u2019ll need this admission ticket on test day. You can take a picture of it, print it, or email it to yourself.\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW241311215 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EArrive on time on test day. Check your admission ticket for your arrival time and the address of your test center.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW241311215 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EBe sure to bring your fully charged device. It\\u2019ll need to stay on for roughly three hours, so we recommend you bring a power cord or portable charger. You\\u2019ll also need your admission ticket, a valid photo ID, and a pencil or pen. Scratch paper will be provided.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW241311215 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EThe digital SAT has two sections\\u2014Reading and Writing, and Math. It should take you just over 2 hours to complete, not including breaks.\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW241311215 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EEach section of the test has two parts called modules, and each module is timed separately. You can move back and forth between questions in a module and review your answers until time expires. There will be a break between sections.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW241311215 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EDuring the test, you\\u2019ll have access to a set of tools.\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW241311215 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EOn all math questions, you\\u2019ll find a reference sheet and a calculator. You can also bring an approved calculator.\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW241311215 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EClick Highlights \\u0026amp; Notes, then select some text to highlight, underline, or leave yourself a note.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW241311215 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EOn multiple-choice questions, if you think an answer option is wrong, you can cross it out.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW241311215 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EYou can use the line reader to help you focus as you\\u2019re reading test content.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW241311215 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EAnd you can mark for review any questions you want to come back to later.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW241311215 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EZoom in and out using keyboard shortcuts on laptops or by pinching on tablets.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW241311215 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EIf you have a problem during the test, click the Help icon for troubleshooting tips. And you can always raise your hand to ask the proctor for help, too.\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW241311215 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EWhen the test is over, your answers will be submitted automatically. Wait until you see the \\u201cCongratulations\\u201d screen to close your device.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW241311215 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EWe\\u2019re excited for you to take the digital SAT. Good luck on test day!\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW241311215 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"SAT\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-01-06T11:12:05-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1767715925\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1841\",\"internal_id\":\"keyboard-sample-spanish\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Sample Sentence: Spanish\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp lang=\\u0022es\\u0022\\u003E\\u00a1Me ir\\u00e1 muy bien en el examen de espa\\u00f1ol!\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222025-10-23T16:50:00-04:00\\u0022\\u003E1761252600\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1851\",\"internal_id\":\"keyboard-sample-chinese\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Sample Sentence: Chinese\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp lang=\\u0022zh\\u0022\\u003E\\u4eca\\u5929\\u7684\\u8003\\u8bd5\\u6211\\u4f1a\\u52a0\\u6cb9\\u7684\\uff01\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222025-10-23T16:50:41-04:00\\u0022\\u003E1761252641\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1836\",\"internal_id\":\"keyboard-sample-english\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Sample Sentence: English\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EI\\u0027m going to do my best on today\\u0027s exam!\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222025-07-31T10:08:07-04:00\\u0022\\u003E1753970887\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1871\",\"internal_id\":\"keyboard-settings\",\"type\":\"help_detail\",\"title\":\"Keyboard Tips\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"body\":\"\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESpecial characters: \\u003C\\/strong\\u003EHold down keys for special characters, such as: \\u00e9, \\u00f1, \\u00bf\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003EInstalling keyboards: \\u003C\\/strong\\u003EIf you don\\u2019t have your foreign language keyboard installed on your device, follow these steps.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cem\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022Apple-tab-span\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E \\u0026nbsp; \\u0026nbsp;Windows\\u003C\\/em\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cul\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cem\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022Apple-tab-span\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/em\\u003EOpen \\u003Cstrong\\u003ESettings \\u003C\\/strong\\u003Ethen go to \\u003Cstrong\\u003ETime \\u0026amp; Language \\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u0026gt; \\u003Cstrong\\u003ELanguage \\u0026amp; region\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EClick \\u003Cstrong\\u003EAdd a language \\u003C\\/strong\\u003Eand select the desired language.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EClick \\u003Cstrong\\u003ENext\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E \\u0026gt; \\u003Cstrong\\u003EInstall\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003C\\/ul\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cem\\u003E\\u0026nbsp; \\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/em\\u003E\\u003Cbr\\u003E\\u003Cem\\u003E\\u0026nbsp; \\u0026nbsp; Mac\\u003C\\/em\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cul\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cem\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022Apple-tab-span\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/em\\u003EOpen the \\u003Cstrong\\u003EApple menu\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E then click \\u003Cstrong\\u003ESystem Settings \\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u0026gt; \\u003Cstrong\\u003EKeyboard\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EClick \\u003Cstrong\\u003EInput Sources \\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u0026gt; \\u003Cstrong\\u003EAdd (+)\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003ESelect the desired language and click \\u003Cstrong\\u003EAdd\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E.\\u003Cbr\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003C\\/ul\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022Apple-tab-span\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E \\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003Cem\\u003EiPad\\u003C\\/em\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cul\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cem\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022Apple-tab-span\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/em\\u003EOpen \\u003Cstrong\\u003ESettings \\u003C\\/strong\\u003Ethen go to \\u003Cstrong\\u003EGeneral \\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u0026gt; \\u003Cstrong\\u003EKeyboard \\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u0026gt; \\u003Cstrong\\u003EKeyboards\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EClick \\u003Cstrong\\u003EAdd New Keyboard \\u003C\\/strong\\u003Eand select the desired language.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003C\\/ul\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp; \\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;\\u003Cbr\\u003E\\u0026nbsp; \\u0026nbsp;\\u003Cem\\u003EChromebook: \\u003C\\/em\\u003EIf you don\\u0027t have a foreign language keyboard installed on your device, please ask someone at your school for help.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESwitching Keyboards: \\u003C\\/strong\\u003EUse shortcuts to switch between English and foreign language keyboards.\\u003Cbr\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cul\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022s1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003EChromebook: \\u003C\\/strong\\u003ECtrl + Shift + Space\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022s1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003EWindows: \\u003C\\/strong\\u003EAlt + Shift\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022s1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003EMac: \\u003C\\/strong\\u003ECtrl + Space\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003EiPad: \\u003C\\/strong\\u003ECtrl + Space \\u003Cem\\u003Eor\\u003C\\/em\\u003E Globe icon\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003C\\/ul\\u003E\",\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222025-11-12T13:27:27-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1762972047\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1856\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-ap-chinese\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThe AP Chinese Language and Culture Exam has 2 sections and lasts approximately 1 hour and 50 minutes.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESection I: Free Response\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThe free-response section of the AP Chinese Language and Culture Exam includes 4 free-response questions and lasts approximately 45 minutes.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESection I, Part A:\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E \\u003Cstrong\\u003ESpeaking\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThis part of the exam includes 2 free-response questions about your project. The part lasts approximately 15 minutes.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESection I, Part B:\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E \\u003Cstrong\\u003EWriting\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThis part of the exam includes 2 free-response questions and lasts approximately 30 minutes. Both questions require written responses in Chinese.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESection II: Multiple Choice\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThe multiple-choice section of the exam includes 2 parts and lasts approximately 1 hour and 5 minutes.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESection II, Part A:\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E \\u003Cstrong\\u003EListening\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThis part of the exam includes 5 question sets, each containing 5 multiple-choice questions, and lasts approximately 25 minutes. Each set includes an audio source that you will use to answer the questions. Once timing for each set expires, you will automatically move on to the next set, and you will be unable to return to the prior set.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESection II, Part B:\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E \\u003Cstrong\\u003EReading\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThis part of the exam includes 6 question sets, each containing 5 multiple-choice questions, and lasts approximately 40 minutes. Each set includes reading material that you will use to answer the questions. Once time expires in this part, all the answers you have already selected will be automatically submitted, and you will be unable to return to the questions.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003ESource materials may have been edited for the purpose of this exam.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThe inclusion of source material in this exam is not intended as an endorsement by College Board of the content, ideas, or values expressed in the material. The sources that appear in the AP Chinese Language and Culture Exam represent a range of different works, as appropriate for measuring the college-level knowledge and skills that are the focus of this course. AP students are not expected or asked to subscribe to any specific cultural or political values, but they are expected to analyze perspectives that may be different from their own and to analyze and interpret sources in their disciplinary contexts.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThere may be references in AP testing materials to companies, products, and brands that are owned by others and subject to trademark law. Neither College Board nor the AP testing materials are affiliated with or endorsed by these trademark owners.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-07-10T17:18:36-04:00\\u0022\\u003E1783718316\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1846\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-ap-spanish-lang\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThe AP Spanish Language and Culture Exam has 2 sections and lasts approximately 2 hours and 30 minutes.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESection I: Free Response\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThe free-response section of the AP Spanish Language and Culture Exam includes 3 free-response questions and lasts approximately 1 hour and 10 minutes.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch3\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESection I, Part A:\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E \\u003Cstrong\\u003ESpeaking\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/h3\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThis part of the exam includes 2 questions about your project. The part lasts approximately 15 minutes.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch3\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESection I, Part B:\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E \\u003Cstrong\\u003EWriting\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/h3\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThis part of the exam includes one free-response question and lasts 55 minutes. During this time, you will review written and audio source materials and write the Argumentative Essay.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESection II: Multiple Choice\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThe multiple-choice section of the exam includes 2 parts and lasts approximately 1 hour and 20 minutes.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch3\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESection II, Part A:\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E \\u003Cstrong\\u003EListening\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/h3\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThis part of the exam includes 5 question sets, each containing 5 multiple-choice questions, and lasts approximately 40 minutes. Each set includes an audio source that you will use to answer the questions. Once timing for each set expires, you will automatically move on to the next set, and you will be unable to return to the prior set.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch3\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESection II, Part B:\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E \\u003Cstrong\\u003EReading\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/h3\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThis part of the exam includes 6 question sets, each containing 5 multiple-choice questions, and lasts approximately 40 minutes. Each set includes reading material that you will use to answer the questions. Once time expires in this part, all the answers you have already selected will be automatically submitted, and you will be unable to return to the questions.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003ESource materials may have been edited for the purpose of this exam.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThe inclusion of source material in this exam is not intended as an endorsement by College Board of the content, ideas, or values expressed in the material. The sources that appear in the AP Spanish Language and Culture Exam represent a range of different works, as appropriate for measuring the college-level knowledge and skills that are the focus of this course. AP students are not expected or asked to subscribe to any specific cultural or political values, but they are expected to analyze perspectives that may be different from their own and to analyze and interpret sources in their disciplinary contexts.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EThere may be references in AP testing materials to companies, products, and brands that are owned by others and subject to trademark law. Neither College Board nor the AP testing materials are affiliated with or endorsed by these trademark owners.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-07-10T17:33:39-04:00\\u0022\\u003E1783719219\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1861\",\"internal_id\":\"microphone-settings\",\"type\":\"help_detail\",\"title\":\"Microphone Tips\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"body\":\"\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EIf your microphone isn\\u2019t working and there\\u2019s another one you can use, please switch and see if that solves the problem.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EOtherwise, try these steps:\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cul\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022s1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003EAlways allow microphone access when using Bluebook.\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022s1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003EMake sure your microphone is fully plugged in and has no frayed or damaged wires.\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022s1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003EConfirm you\\u2019ve selected the correct microphone under \\u003Cstrong\\u003EKeyboards \\u0026amp; Audio\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E.\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003ECheck that your volume isn\\u2019t muted\\/turned down.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003C\\/ul\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ETo allow microphone access, you may need to adjust your settings.\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003E\\u003Cem\\u003EOn a Windows device:\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/em\\u003E\\u003Cbr\\u003EGo to \\u003Cstrong\\u003ESettings\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E \\u0026gt; \\u003Cstrong\\u003EPrivacy \\u0026amp; Security\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E \\u0026gt; \\u003Cstrong\\u003EMicrophone\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E \\u0026gt; Enable \\u003Cstrong\\u003ELet desktop apps access your microphone\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003E\\u003Cem\\u003EOn a Mac device:\\u003C\\/em\\u003E\\u003Cbr\\u003EGo to \\u003Cstrong\\u003ESettings\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E \\u0026gt; \\u003Cstrong\\u003EPrivacy \\u0026amp; Security\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E \\u0026gt; \\u003Cstrong\\u003EMicrophone\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E \\u0026gt; Enable \\u003Cstrong\\u003EBluebook\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003E\\u003Cem\\u003EOn an iPad:\\u003C\\/em\\u003E\\u003Cbr\\u003EGo to \\u003Cstrong\\u003ESettings\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E \\u0026gt; \\u003Cstrong\\u003EApps \\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u0026gt; \\u003Cstrong\\u003EBluebook \\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u0026gt; Allow \\u003Cstrong\\u003EMicrophone\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003E\\u003Cem\\u003EOn a Chromebook:\\u003C\\/em\\u003E\\u003Cbr\\u003EContact someone at your school for help.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\",\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222025-11-14T09:23:07-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1763130187\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1866\",\"internal_id\":\"headphone-settings\",\"type\":\"help_detail\",\"title\":\"Headphone Tips\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"body\":\"\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EIf your headphones aren\\u2019t working and there\\u2019s another set you can use, please switch and see if that solves the problem.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EOtherwise, try these steps:\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cul\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022s1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003EAlways allow headphones access when using Bluebook.\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022s1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003EMake sure your headphones are fully plugged in and have no frayed or damaged wires.\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022s1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003EConfirm you\\u2019ve selected the correct headphones under \\u003Cstrong\\u003EAudio Settings\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E.\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003ECheck that your volume isn\\u2019t muted\\/turned down.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003C\\/ul\\u003E\",\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222025-11-03T11:41:12-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1762188072\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1876\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-test-help-audio\",\"type\":\"profile_collection\",\"title\":\"Troubleshooting Tips\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"help_items\":[{\"id\":\"1866\",\"title\":\"Headphone Tips\",\"body\":\"\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EIf your headphones aren\\u2019t working and there\\u2019s another set you can use, please switch and see if that solves the problem.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EOtherwise, try these steps:\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cul\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022s1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003EAlways allow headphones access when using Bluebook.\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022s1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003EMake sure your headphones are fully plugged in and have no frayed or damaged wires.\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022s1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003EConfirm you\\u2019ve selected the correct headphones under \\u003Cstrong\\u003EAudio Settings\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E.\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003ECheck that your volume isn\\u2019t muted\\/turned down.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003C\\/ul\\u003E\",\"audience\":[\"\\u003Ca href=\\u0022\\/taxonomy\\/term\\/25\\u0022 hreflang=\\u0022en\\u0022\\u003EStudents\\u003C\\/a\\u003E\"],\"offering\":[\"\\u003Ca href=\\u0022\\/taxonomy\\/term\\/51\\u0022 hreflang=\\u0022en\\u0022\\u003EAP\\u003C\\/a\\u003E\"],\"suppress_faq_view\":\"Off\"},{\"id\":\"1861\",\"title\":\"Microphone Tips\",\"body\":\"\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EIf your microphone isn\\u2019t working and there\\u2019s another one you can use, please switch and see if that solves the problem.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EOtherwise, try these steps:\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cul\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022s1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003EAlways allow microphone access when using Bluebook.\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022s1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003EMake sure your microphone is fully plugged in and has no frayed or damaged wires.\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022s1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003EConfirm you\\u2019ve selected the correct microphone under \\u003Cstrong\\u003EKeyboards \\u0026amp; Audio\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E.\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003ECheck that your volume isn\\u2019t muted\\/turned down.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003C\\/ul\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ETo allow microphone access, you may need to adjust your settings.\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003E\\u003Cem\\u003EOn a Windows device:\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/em\\u003E\\u003Cbr\\u003EGo to \\u003Cstrong\\u003ESettings\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E \\u0026gt; \\u003Cstrong\\u003EPrivacy \\u0026amp; Security\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E \\u0026gt; \\u003Cstrong\\u003EMicrophone\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E \\u0026gt; Enable \\u003Cstrong\\u003ELet desktop apps access your microphone\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003E\\u003Cem\\u003EOn a Mac device:\\u003C\\/em\\u003E\\u003Cbr\\u003EGo to \\u003Cstrong\\u003ESettings\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E \\u0026gt; \\u003Cstrong\\u003EPrivacy \\u0026amp; Security\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E \\u0026gt; \\u003Cstrong\\u003EMicrophone\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E \\u0026gt; Enable \\u003Cstrong\\u003EBluebook\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003E\\u003Cem\\u003EOn an iPad:\\u003C\\/em\\u003E\\u003Cbr\\u003EGo to \\u003Cstrong\\u003ESettings\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E \\u0026gt; \\u003Cstrong\\u003EApps \\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u0026gt; \\u003Cstrong\\u003EBluebook \\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u0026gt; Allow \\u003Cstrong\\u003EMicrophone\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003E\\u003Cem\\u003EOn a Chromebook:\\u003C\\/em\\u003E\\u003Cbr\\u003EContact someone at your school for help.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\",\"audience\":[\"\\u003Ca href=\\u0022\\/taxonomy\\/term\\/25\\u0022 hreflang=\\u0022en\\u0022\\u003EStudents\\u003C\\/a\\u003E\"],\"offering\":[\"\\u003Ca href=\\u0022\\/taxonomy\\/term\\/51\\u0022 hreflang=\\u0022en\\u0022\\u003EAP\\u003C\\/a\\u003E\"],\"suppress_faq_view\":\"Off\"},{\"id\":\"1871\",\"title\":\"Keyboard Tips\",\"body\":\"\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESpecial characters: \\u003C\\/strong\\u003EHold down keys for special characters, such as: \\u00e9, \\u00f1, \\u00bf\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003EInstalling keyboards: \\u003C\\/strong\\u003EIf you don\\u2019t have your foreign language keyboard installed on your device, follow these steps.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cem\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022Apple-tab-span\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E \\u0026nbsp; \\u0026nbsp;Windows\\u003C\\/em\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cul\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cem\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022Apple-tab-span\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/em\\u003EOpen \\u003Cstrong\\u003ESettings \\u003C\\/strong\\u003Ethen go to \\u003Cstrong\\u003ETime \\u0026amp; Language \\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u0026gt; \\u003Cstrong\\u003ELanguage \\u0026amp; region\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EClick \\u003Cstrong\\u003EAdd a language \\u003C\\/strong\\u003Eand select the desired language.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EClick \\u003Cstrong\\u003ENext\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E \\u0026gt; \\u003Cstrong\\u003EInstall\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003C\\/ul\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cem\\u003E\\u0026nbsp; \\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/em\\u003E\\u003Cbr\\u003E\\u003Cem\\u003E\\u0026nbsp; \\u0026nbsp; Mac\\u003C\\/em\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cul\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cem\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022Apple-tab-span\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/em\\u003EOpen the \\u003Cstrong\\u003EApple menu\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E then click \\u003Cstrong\\u003ESystem Settings \\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u0026gt; \\u003Cstrong\\u003EKeyboard\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EClick \\u003Cstrong\\u003EInput Sources \\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u0026gt; \\u003Cstrong\\u003EAdd (+)\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003ESelect the desired language and click \\u003Cstrong\\u003EAdd\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E.\\u003Cbr\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003C\\/ul\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022Apple-tab-span\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E \\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003Cem\\u003EiPad\\u003C\\/em\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cul\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cem\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022Apple-tab-span\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/em\\u003EOpen \\u003Cstrong\\u003ESettings \\u003C\\/strong\\u003Ethen go to \\u003Cstrong\\u003EGeneral \\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u0026gt; \\u003Cstrong\\u003EKeyboard \\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u0026gt; \\u003Cstrong\\u003EKeyboards\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EClick \\u003Cstrong\\u003EAdd New Keyboard \\u003C\\/strong\\u003Eand select the desired language.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003C\\/ul\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp; \\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;\\u003Cbr\\u003E\\u0026nbsp; \\u0026nbsp;\\u003Cem\\u003EChromebook: \\u003C\\/em\\u003EIf you don\\u0027t have a foreign language keyboard installed on your device, please ask someone at your school for help.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESwitching Keyboards: \\u003C\\/strong\\u003EUse shortcuts to switch between English and foreign language keyboards.\\u003Cbr\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cul\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022s1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003EChromebook: \\u003C\\/strong\\u003ECtrl + Shift + Space\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022s1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003EWindows: \\u003C\\/strong\\u003EAlt + Shift\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022s1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003EMac: \\u003C\\/strong\\u003ECtrl + Space\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003EiPad: \\u003C\\/strong\\u003ECtrl + Space \\u003Cem\\u003Eor\\u003C\\/em\\u003E Globe icon\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003C\\/ul\\u003E\",\"audience\":[\"\\u003Ca href=\\u0022\\/taxonomy\\/term\\/25\\u0022 hreflang=\\u0022en\\u0022\\u003EStudents\\u003C\\/a\\u003E\"],\"offering\":[\"\\u003Ca href=\\u0022\\/taxonomy\\/term\\/51\\u0022 hreflang=\\u0022en\\u0022\\u003EAP\\u003C\\/a\\u003E\"],\"suppress_faq_view\":\"Off\"}],\"offering\":\"\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222025-08-20T15:11:07-04:00\\u0022\\u003E1755717067\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1831\",\"internal_id\":\"tools-video-transcript\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Testing Tools\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW73592437 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EThis video is silent. \\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW73592437 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW73592437 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun MacChromeBold SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ESection Directions: \\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EDirections are on the top left of each test screen.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022sr-only\\u0022\\u003E Find the show directions button in the exam player controls section.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW73592437 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW73592437 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun MacChromeBold SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ETesting Timer: \\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EUse the timer to pace yourself. You can hide it \\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun ContextualSpellingAndGrammarErrorV2Themed\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003Euntil\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003E 5 minutes remain.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022sr-only\\u0022\\u003E The hide\\/show buttons are in the timer section.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW73592437 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW73592437 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun MacChromeBold SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003EHighlights \\u0026amp; Notes: \\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EClick Highlights \\u0026amp; Notes then select some text to get started.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022sr-only\\u0022\\u003E The Highlights \\u0026amp; Notes button is in the test tools section. When activated, you can highlight text within the exam and create notes from the Highlight Options group of controls.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW73592437 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW73592437 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun MacChromeBold SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ELine Reader: \\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EUse the line reader to help you focus as you\\u0027re reading test content.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022sr-only\\u0022\\u003E Access the line reader from the More options region within the test tools section.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW73592437 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW73592437 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun MacChromeBold SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ECalculator: \\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun CommentStart\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EOn the SAT Suite of Assessments and certain AP Exams\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003E, you\\u0027ll have access to a calculator. Some exams have more than one kind.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022sr-only\\u0022\\u003EThe calculator and reference buttons are located in the test tools section. When activated, a region for the calculator or reference sheets is opened.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW73592437 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW73592437 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun MacChromeBold SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003EReference Sheet: \\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EMany exams have a reference sheet where you can find common formulas.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW73592437 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW73592437 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun MacChromeBold SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003EHelp: \\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EClick on More to access help content.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022sr-only\\u0022\\u003E Access the More button and expanded options from the test tools section.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW73592437 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW73592437 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun MacChromeBold SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003EExpand Left\\/Right: \\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EGrab the center line to \\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun ContextualSpellingAndGrammarErrorV2Themed\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003Eexpand\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003E either side of the screen.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022sr-only\\u0022\\u003E The separator control to expand the left and right panels is named \\u0022resize page content\\u0022 and located between the passage and question regions of the page.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW73592437 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW73592437 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun MacChromeBold SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003EZoom: \\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EZoom with keyboard shortcuts on laptops or by pinching on tablets.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW73592437 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW73592437 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun MacChromeBold SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003EMark for Review: \\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EUse the bookmark icon to flag any question you want to come back to. \\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022sr-only\\u0022\\u003EThe mark for review button is located in the Question and Answer section.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW73592437 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW73592437 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun MacChromeBold SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003EOption Eliminator: \\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EOn multiple-choice questions, if you think an answer option is wrong, you can cross it out.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022sr-only\\u0022\\u003E The option eliminator push button is located in the Question and Answer section. When pressed, buttons to cross out or undo crossed-out options appear adjacent to each answer option.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW73592437 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022Paragraph SCXW73592437 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun MacChromeBold SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003EQuestion Menu: \\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun ContextualSpellingAndGrammarErrorV2Themed\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003ENavigate to\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun SCXW73592437 BCX0 NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003E any question in the module or part.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022sr-only\\u0022\\u003E The question navigator button is in the Question navigation section. When expanded, the bookmark icon will appear in the question navigator to indicate questions that have been marked for review.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW73592437 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP, SAT\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-02-25T14:57:52-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1772049472\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1821\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-sat-essay-linear\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Test Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EThe SAT with Essay has three sections: Reading and Writing, Math, and the Essay.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ESection 1: Reading and Writing (66 Questions)\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThere are two modules in the Reading and Writing section. Each module has 33 questions.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ESection 2: Math (54 Questions)\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThere are two modules in the Math section. Each module has 27 questions.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ESection 3: Essay\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThere is one module in the Essay section.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003EModules\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EWithin each section, the modules are timed separately. If time permits, you can review your answers in a given module. When the timer reaches zero, you will automatically move on. Once you move on from any module, you cannot return to it.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003EDirections\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EDirections for answering the questions appear at the start of each section. You can find these directions at the top-left corner of every question screen.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"SAT\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-01-15T15:52:02-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1768510322\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1816\",\"internal_id\":\"exam-builder-tooltip-code-209\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Text-to-Speech (Embedded)\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003E\\u003Cspan\\u003EIf you\\u2019re approved for text-to-speech, use this tool on test day to hear entire passages or specific sentences.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222025-02-04T17:09:38-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1738706978\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1826\",\"internal_id\":\"section-break-ap-hybrid-practice\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Test Preview Break\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EYou can \\u003Cspan data-ssml-sub-alias=\\u0022\\u201crezoom\\u201d\\u0022\\u003Eresume\\u003C\\/span\\u003E this practice test as soon as you\\u2019re ready to move on. On test day, you\\u2019ll wait until the clock counts down. Read below to see how breaks work on test day.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\",\"id\":\"section-break-ap-hybrid-practice-p1\",\"title\":\"Test Preview Break\"},{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EPlace your exam booklet on your desk now.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003EFollow these rules during the break:\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Col\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003EDo not disturb students who are still testing.\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003EDo not exit the app or close your laptop.\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003EDo not access\\u0026nbsp;phones, smartwatches, textbooks, notes, or the internet.\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003EDo not eat or drink in the test room.\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003EDo not speak in the test room; outside the test room, do not discuss the exam with anyone.\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003C\\/ol\\u003E\",\"id\":\"section-break-ap-hybrid-practice-p2\",\"title\":\"Take a Break: Do Not Close Your Device\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222025-06-05T13:18:11-04:00\\u0022\\u003E1749143891\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1811\",\"internal_id\":\"proctor-instrux-ap-hybrid\",\"type\":\"help_detail\",\"title\":\"Verbal Instructions: Hybrid\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"body\":\"\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E[\\u003Cem\\u003ENote: These instructions may vary slightly from what the proctor reads.\\u003C\\/em\\u003E]\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003EYour proctor will read this aloud:\\u202f\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EWelcome. If you\\u0026nbsp;haven\\u2019t\\u0026nbsp;completed check-in yet, pause while I read. You can finish checking in later.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EToday\\u0026nbsp;you\\u2019re\\u0026nbsp;taking a digital AP Exam. The exam has two sections with a break in between. This is a hybrid digital exam, so each section works differently, so listen carefully.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003ESection I is multiple\\u0026nbsp;choice, and\\u0026nbsp;you\\u2019ll\\u0026nbsp;use Bluebook on your device to read the exam questions and enter your answers. Section II is free response;\\u0026nbsp;you\\u2019ll\\u0026nbsp;still read the questions in Bluebook but write your answers in the free-response booklet.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003ERemember, you agreed to follow rules preventing students from having an unfair advantage. I will dismiss anyone who tries to break those rules, and their scores will be canceled. They may also be prevented from taking College Board exams in the future.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EBluebook should be the only application open on your device unless\\u0026nbsp;you\\u2019re\\u0026nbsp;using approved assistive technology. Close all other applications now. You might need to quit Bluebook first and reopen it when you finish.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EYou should have the following items on your desk:\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cul\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022s1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003EYour\\u0026nbsp;testing device\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022s1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E2 black or dark blue pens or No. 2 pencils\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022s1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003EA free-response booklet\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022s1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003EYour AP ID label sheet\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022s1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E2 sheets of scratch paper\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022s1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003EAn\\u0026nbsp;exam-specific reference information booklet [\\u003Cem\\u003Enot applicable for Calculus, Macroeconomics, or Microeconomics\\u003C\\/em\\u003E]\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003C\\/ul\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cbr\\u003EMake sure your free-response booklet has the name of this exam and today\\u2019s date on the front cover.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EWhen using your printed reference information booklet, you may use the margins or any blank space for scratch\\u0026nbsp;work\\u0026nbsp;as well.\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EYou\\u2019re\\u0026nbsp;allowed\\u0026nbsp;2 handheld calculators. Store your backup calculator under your desk. You may also use the built-in Desmos calculator available in Bluebook. In Section II,\\u0026nbsp;you\\u2019ll\\u0026nbsp;need a pen or pencil to write your\\u0026nbsp;responses. If you use a pencil, be sure that your writing is dark enough to read easily. To avoid scoring problems,\\u0026nbsp;don\\u2019t\\u0026nbsp;write in multiple colors.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003ENow, check that your AP ID label sheet has your name printed at the top.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003ERaise your hand if\\u0026nbsp;you need a pen or pencil or if\\u0026nbsp;there are\\u0026nbsp;any issues with your materials.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EIn Section II,\\u0026nbsp;you\\u2019ll\\u0026nbsp;need a pen or pencil to write your responses. If you use a pencil, be sure that your writing is dark enough to read easily. To avoid scoring problems,\\u0026nbsp;don\\u2019t\\u0026nbsp;write in multiple colors.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003ENow, check that your AP ID label sheet has your name printed at the top.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003ERaise your hand if you need a pen or pencil or if there are any issues with your materials.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EYou should also have 2 sheets of scratch paper, which\\u0026nbsp;I\\u2019ll\\u0026nbsp;collect after the exam, so\\u0026nbsp;don\\u2019t\\u0026nbsp;tear\\u0026nbsp;them. Now,\\u0026nbsp;write your full name, today\\u2019s date, and the exam name in the top right corner\\u0026nbsp;of\\u0026nbsp;both\\u0026nbsp;sheets.\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EYou can use the scratch paper for notes and planning your responses,\\u0026nbsp;but no credit will be given for anything written on scratch paper.\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EIn Section II, your\\u0026nbsp;answers\\u0026nbsp;and any work\\u0026nbsp;you\\u2019re\\u0026nbsp;asked to show must be written in the free-response booklet, as specified in the directions in Bluebook.\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003ENow\\u0026nbsp;it\\u2019s\\u0026nbsp;time to label your free-response booklet. Listen carefully to my instructions.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EFirst, complete the information on the front cover. For step 3, you\\u2019ll need your school code; it\\u2019s printed in the top right corner of your AP ID label sheet.\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003ENext, place an AP ID label in the space provided and read the information on the right. Look up when you finish.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EMake sure the subject listed on your reference information booklets matches the exam you\\u2019re taking. Write your name in the space provided on the cover of the booklet, and write the date next to it.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EAre there any questions?\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003EThen your proctor will read this:\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E[\\u003Cem\\u003EFor Physics and Chemistry only:\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/em\\u003EIn Section II, the free-response section, the questions in Bluebook include instructions telling you which page in your booklet to write your answers on. Make sure you write your answers on the correct page in the booklet.]\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E[\\u003Cem\\u003EFor Macroeconomics or Microeconomics only:\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/em\\u003EIn Section II, the free-response section, start your response to each question on a new page. At the top of each page, fill in the circle for the question number\\u0026nbsp;you\\u2019re\\u0026nbsp;answering on that page. If you fill in the wrong circle, cross it out neatly with an X, and fill in the correct circle.]\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EWhen you use the free-response booklet\\u0026nbsp;during Section II, make sure you write your answers in the correct place. If you start to answer on the wrong page, you may cross it out and write it on the correct page.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EMake sure to keep an eye on the timer in Bluebook while writing and stop when time runs out.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EIf you run out of space, raise your hand\\u0026nbsp;and\\u0026nbsp;I\\u2019ll\\u0026nbsp;give you extra paper.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E[\\u003Cem\\u003EFor Calculus only:\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/em\\u003ENow listen carefully to these calculator rules:\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cul\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022s1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003ESections I and II both have\\u0026nbsp;a part\\u0026nbsp;A and\\u0026nbsp;a part\\u0026nbsp;B.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022s1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003EThere\\u2019s\\u0026nbsp;a 1-minute pause between\\u0026nbsp;parts.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022s1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003EIn each section, graphing calculators are needed in one part and prohibited in the other.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022s1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003EYou\\u2019ll\\u0026nbsp;see reminders in Bluebook and your free-response booklet whenever calculators are prohibited.\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022s1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003EYou can use your own calculator or the one available in Bluebook.]\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003C\\/ul\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003Cbr\\u003EAre there any questions?\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003EThen your proctor will read this:\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EPlace your free-response booklet under your chair and leave it there until your break. Leave your AP ID label sheet on your desk so I can collect it.\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EI\\u2019ll\\u0026nbsp;come around now to make sure you cleared your desk as instructed in Bluebook. And if you\\u0026nbsp;brought\\u0026nbsp;a calculator,\\u0026nbsp;I\\u2019ll\\u0026nbsp;make sure\\u0026nbsp;it\\u2019s\\u0026nbsp;acceptable.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EIf you still have prohibited items, turn them off and put them on your desk so I can collect them.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003EAfter your proctor checks student desks,\\u0026nbsp;they\\u2019ll\\u0026nbsp;read this:\\u202f\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EPlease give me your attention again.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EBluebook will end Section I and start your break automatically.\\u0026nbsp;You might start your break at slightly different times than your neighbor, so please be quiet at all times.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EWhen your break starts, leave your calculator on your desk and place your free-response booklet on your desk.\\u0026nbsp;Don\\u2019t\\u0026nbsp;take your booklet,\\u0026nbsp;calculator, or scratch paper\\u0026nbsp;out of the room.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EWhen your break ends, click\\u0026nbsp;\\u003Cstrong\\u003EResume Testing\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;and take a few minutes to read the Section II directions before you click\\u0026nbsp;\\u003Cstrong\\u003EResume Testing\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/strong\\u003Eagain and start your timer.\\u0026nbsp;I\\u2019m\\u0026nbsp;going to repeat that important tip: to save testing time, read the free-response directions before your countdown clock starts.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003ETo take a break at any other time, go to the\\u0026nbsp;\\u003Cstrong\\u003EMore\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;menu and click\\u0026nbsp;\\u003Cstrong\\u003EUnscheduled Break\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E. Raise your hand and wait for me to dismiss you if you want to leave the room.\\u0026nbsp;You\\u2019ll\\u0026nbsp;lose testing time if you take an unscheduled break.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EIf you have an approved accommodation for breaks as needed, select\\u0026nbsp;\\u003Cstrong\\u003EPause\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;under the timer so you\\u0026nbsp;don\\u2019t\\u0026nbsp;lose testing time.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EI\\u2019ll give you the start code after I read these final instructions.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EIf you see\\u202fthe low-battery warning on\\u202fyour\\u202fscreen, raise your hand so I can help you.\\u0026nbsp;Keep your laptop open or your tablet uncovered until I dismiss you.\\u0026nbsp;I\\u2019ve\\u0026nbsp;written a reminder here.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EWhen your exam ends, sit quietly until I make sure your answers were submitted and collect your materials. Remember that others may still be testing.\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003ERaise your hand at any time if you need help\\u0026nbsp;or more scratch\\u0026nbsp;paper. In Section II, raise your hand if you need extra paper to finish writing your response.\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E[\\u003Cem\\u003EFor\\u0026nbsp;Calculus\\u0026nbsp;only:\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/em\\u003ENow, place your calculators\\u0026nbsp;under your desk and leave\\u0026nbsp;them\\u0026nbsp;there until Section I Part B.]\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EAre\\u0026nbsp;there\\u0026nbsp;any questions?\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003EAfter your proctor pauses to answer questions,\\u0026nbsp;they\\u2019ll\\u0026nbsp;read this:\\u202f\\u202f\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EWhen you enter the code and click\\u0026nbsp;\\u003Cstrong\\u003EStart Test\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E, your timer will start and you can begin testing.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EIf you\\u0026nbsp;don\\u2019t see\\u0026nbsp;the start code screen yet, finish checking in.\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp class=\\u0022p1\\u0022\\u003EI\\u2019ll\\u0026nbsp;read the start code now and write it on the board. Good luck!\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\",\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-03-10T16:07:46-04:00\\u0022\\u003E1773173266\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1806\",\"internal_id\":\"early-exit\",\"type\":\"help_detail\",\"title\":\"Ending the Test Early\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"body\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TrackChangeTextInsertion TrackedChange SCXW189689575 BCX0 TextRun NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003EIf you\\u0027re approved for extra time, you can move on from a section or end the test before your full time expires, though we encourage you to use extra time to check your work. You must use the standard time for a section before you can move on. When the standard time has elapsed, the \\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TrackChangeTextInsertion TrackedChange SCXW189689575 BCX0 TextRun MacChromeBold NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ENext \\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TrackChangeTextInsertion TrackedChange SCXW189689575 BCX0 TextRun NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003Ebutton on the \\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TrackChangeTextInsertion TrackedChange SCXW189689575 BCX0 TextRun MacChromeBold NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003ECheck Your Work \\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TrackChangeTextInsertion TrackedChange SCXW189689575 BCX0 TextRun NormalTextRun\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003Epage will become active. Once you move on from any section of the test, you cannot go back.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022TextRun EmptyTextRun SCXW189689575 BCX0\\u0022 lang=\\u0022EN-US\\u0022\\u003E\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003Cspan class=\\u0022EOP SCXW189689575 BCX0\\u0022\\u003E\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\",\"offering\":\"AP, SAT\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222024-11-20T16:42:28-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1732138948\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1801\",\"internal_id\":\"login-bb-offline-error\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Bluebook Is Temporarily Unavailable\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EThe application will be offline for a short while. Please try again later.\\u0026nbsp;\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"SAT\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222025-01-06T16:25:26-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1736198726\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1766\",\"internal_id\":\"section-break-ap-hybrid\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Take a Break: Do Not Close Your Device\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003E\\u003Cspan\\u003EPlace your exam booklet on your desk now.\\u003C\\/span\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003EFollow these rules during the break:\\u003C\\/strong\\u003E\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Col\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003EDo not disturb students who are still testing.\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003EDo not exit the\\u0026nbsp;app or close your laptop.\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003EDo not access phones, smartwatches, textbooks, notes, or the internet.\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003EDo not eat or drink in the test room.\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003Cli\\u003EDo not speak in the test room; outside the test room, do not discuss the exam with anyone.\\u003C\\/li\\u003E\\u003C\\/ol\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222025-01-06T14:41:22-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1736192482\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1466\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-ck-cyber-day2\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Day 2 Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EDay 2 of the CK Cybersecurity 1: Networking Fundamentals Exam consists of a multiple-choice section.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003EMultiple Choice\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThis section has 36 questions and lasts 1 hour. This section represents 50% of your total score. Your score on this section is based on the number of questions answered correctly. Points are not deducted for incorrect answers or unanswered questions.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ETaking the Exam\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EYou can go back and forth between questions in the section until time expires. The clock will turn red when 5 minutes remain\\u2014\\u003Cem\\u003Ethe proctor will not give you any time updates or warnings\\u003C\\/em\\u003E. Once time expires in the section, you cannot return to it.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EYou may use scratch paper for notes and planning, but credit will only be given for responses entered in this application. Any text you enter as an annotation will \\u003Cem\\u003Enot\\u003C\\/em\\u003E be included in your answer submissions. When time expires in the section, all answers you have already entered will be submitted.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThere may be references in AP testing materials to companies, products, and brands that are owned by others and subject to trademark law. Neither College Board nor the AP testing materials are affiliated with or endorsed by these trademark owners.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222025-03-06T14:59:52-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1741291192\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1461\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-ck-cyber-day1\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Day 1 Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EDay 1 of the CK Cybersecurity 1: Networking Fundamentals Exam consists of a multiple-choice section.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003EMultiple Choice\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThis section has 36 questions and lasts 1 hour. This section represents 50% of your total score. Your score on this section is based on the number of questions answered correctly. Points are not deducted for incorrect answers or unanswered questions.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ETaking the Exam\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EYou can go back and forth between questions in the section until time expires. The clock will turn red when 5 minutes remain\\u2014\\u003Cem\\u003Ethe proctor will not give you any time updates or warnings\\u003C\\/em\\u003E. Once time expires in the section, you cannot return to it.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EYou may use scratch paper for notes and planning, but credit will only be given for responses entered in this application. Any text you enter as an annotation will \\u003Cem\\u003Enot\\u003C\\/em\\u003E\\u003Cstrong\\u003E \\u003C\\/strong\\u003Ebe included in your answer submissions. When time expires in the section, all answers you have already entered will be submitted.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThere may be references in AP testing materials to companies, products, and brands that are owned by others and subject to trademark law. Neither College Board nor the AP testing materials are affiliated with or endorsed by these trademark owners.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222025-03-06T15:00:26-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1741291226\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1471\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-ck-cyber\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EThe CK Cybersecurity 1: Networking Fundamentals Exam has 2 multiple-choice sections and lasts 2 hours.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ESection I: Multiple Choice\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThe first multiple-choice section has 36 questions and lasts 1 hour. This section represents 50% of your total score. Your score on this section is based on the number of questions answered correctly. Points are not deducted for incorrect answers or unanswered questions.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ESection II: Multiple Choice\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThe second multiple-choice section has 36 questions and lasts 1 hour. This section represents 50% of your total score. Your score on this section is based on the number of questions answered correctly. Points are not deducted for incorrect answers or unanswered questions.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ETaking the Exam\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EEach section is timed separately. You can go back and forth between questions in a section until time expires. The clock will turn red when 5 minutes remain in the section\\u2014\\u003Cem\\u003Ethe proctor will not give you any time updates or warnings\\u003C\\/em\\u003E. You cannot move ahead to a different section. Once time expires in a section, you cannot return to it.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EYou may use scratch paper for notes and planning, but credit will only be given for responses entered in this application. Any text you enter as an annotation will \\u003Cem\\u003Enot\\u003C\\/em\\u003E be included in your answer submissions. When time expires in a section, all answers you have already entered will be submitted.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThere may be references in AP testing materials to companies, products, and brands that are owned by others and subject to trademark law. Neither College Board nor the AP testing materials are affiliated with or endorsed by these trademark owners.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222025-03-06T14:58:59-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1741291139\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1596\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-ap-phys-c-mech-day2\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Day 2 Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EDay 2 of the AP Physics C: Mechanics Exam consists of the multiple-choice section.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003EMultiple Choice\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThe multiple-choice section has 40 questions and lasts 1 hour and 20 minutes. This section represents 50% of your total score. Your score on the multiple-choice section is based on the number of questions answered correctly. Points are not deducted for incorrect answers or unanswered questions.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ETaking the Exam\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EYou can go back and forth between questions in the section until time expires. The clock will turn red when 5 minutes remain\\u2014\\u003Cem\\u003Ethe proctor will not give you any time updates or warnings\\u003C\\/em\\u003E. Once time expires in the section, you cannot return to it.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EA calculator and reference information, including lists of equations, are available in this application and can be accessed throughout the exam.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EYou may use scratch paper for notes and planning, but credit will only be given for responses entered in this application. When time expires in the section, all answers you have already entered will be submitted.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThere may be references in AP testing materials to companies, products, and brands that are owned by others and subject to trademark law. Neither College Board nor the AP testing materials are affiliated with or endorsed by these trademark owners.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222025-01-06T14:38:14-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1736192294\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1641\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-ap-phys-c-mech-day1\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Day 1 Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EDay 1 of the AP Physics C: Mechanics Exam consists of the free-response section.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003EFree Response\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThe free-response section has 4 questions and lasts 1 hour and 40 minutes. This section represents 50% of your total score. Questions 1 and 3 are worth 10 points each. Question 2 is worth 12 points. Question 4 is worth 8 points.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ETaking the Exam\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EYou can go back and forth between questions in the section until time expires. The clock will turn red when 5 minutes remain\\u2014\\u003Cem\\u003Ethe proctor will not give you any time updates or warnings\\u003C\\/em\\u003E. Once time expires in the section, you cannot return to it.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EA calculator and reference information, including lists of equations, are available in this application and can be accessed throughout the exam.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThe free-response questions are in this application, but you must write your responses to the questions in the free-response booklet. Use a pencil or pen with black or dark blue ink. You may use the available paper for scratch work, but credit will only be given for responses that are written in the free-response booklet.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThere may be references in AP testing materials to companies, products, and brands that are owned by others and subject to trademark law. Neither College Board nor the AP testing materials are affiliated with or endorsed by these trademark owners.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222025-01-06T14:39:02-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1736192342\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1636\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-ap-phys-c-mech\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EThe AP Physics C: Mechanics Exam has 2 sections and lasts 3 hours.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ESection I: Multiple Choice\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThe multiple-choice section has 40 questions and lasts 1 hour and 20 minutes. This section represents 50% of your total score. Your score on the multiple-choice section is based on the number of questions answered correctly. Points are not deducted for incorrect answers or unanswered questions.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ESection II: Free Response\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThe free-response section has 4 questions and lasts 1 hour and 40 minutes. This section represents 50% of your total score. Questions 1 and 3 are worth 10 points each. Question 2 is worth 12 points. Question 4 is worth 8 points.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ETaking the Exam\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EEach section is timed separately. You can go back and forth between questions in a section until time expires. The clock will turn red when 5 minutes remain in the section\\u2014\\u003Cem\\u003Ethe proctor will not give you any time updates or warnings\\u003C\\/em\\u003E. You cannot move ahead to a different section. Once time expires in a section, you cannot return to it.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EA calculator and reference information, including lists of equations, are available in this application and can be accessed throughout the exam.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EYou may use the available paper for scratch work, but credit for Section I: Multiple Choice will only be given for responses entered in this application. When time expires in a section, all answers you have already entered will be submitted.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EFor Section II: Free Response, the questions are in this application, but you must write your responses to the questions in the free-response booklet. Use a pencil or pen with black or dark blue ink. You may use the available paper for scratch work, but credit will only be given for responses that are written in the free-response booklet.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThere may be references in AP testing materials to companies, products, and brands that are owned by others and subject to trademark law. Neither College Board nor the AP testing materials are affiliated with or endorsed by these trademark owners.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222025-01-06T14:39:02-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1736192342\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1611\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-ap-chem-day2\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Day 2 Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EDay 2 of the AP Chemistry Exam consists of the multiple-choice section.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003EMultiple Choice\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThe multiple-choice section has 60 questions and lasts 1 hour and 30 minutes. This section represents 50% of your total score. Your score on the multiple-choice section is based on the number of questions answered correctly. Points are not deducted for incorrect answers or unanswered questions.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ETaking the Exam\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EYou can go back and forth between questions in the section until time expires. The clock will turn red when 5 minutes remain\\u2014\\u003Cem\\u003Ethe proctor will not give you any time updates or warnings\\u003C\\/em\\u003E. Once time expires in the section, you cannot return to it.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EA calculator and reference information, including a periodic table and lists of equations and constants, are available in this application and can be accessed throughout the exam.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EYou may use scratch paper for notes and planning, but credit will only be given for responses entered in this application. When time expires in the section, all answers you have already entered will be submitted.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThere may be references in AP testing materials to companies, products, and brands that are owned by others and subject to trademark law. Neither College Board nor the AP testing materials are affiliated with or endorsed by these trademark owners.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222025-01-06T14:38:14-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1736192294\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1686\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-ap-chem-day1\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Day 1 Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EDay 1 of the AP Chemistry Exam consists of the free-response section.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003EFree Response\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThe free-response section has 7 questions and lasts 1 hour and 45 minutes. This section represents 50% of your total score. Questions 1 through 3 are long free-response questions, each worth 10 points. Questions 4 through 7 are short free-response questions, each worth 4 points.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ETaking the Exam\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EYou can go back and forth between questions in the section until time expires. The clock will turn red when 5 minutes remain\\u2014\\u003Cem\\u003Ethe proctor will not give you any time updates or warnings\\u003C\\/em\\u003E. Once time expires in the section, you cannot return to it.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EA calculator and reference information, including a periodic table and lists of equations and constants, are available in this application and can be accessed throughout the exam.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThe free-response questions are in this application, but you must write your responses to the questions in the free-response booklet. Use a pencil or pen with black or dark blue ink. You may use the available paper for scratch work, but credit will only be given for responses that are written in the free-response booklet.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThere may be references in AP testing materials to companies, products, and brands that are owned by others and subject to trademark law. Neither College Board nor the AP testing materials are affiliated with or endorsed by these trademark owners.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222025-01-06T14:39:54-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1736192394\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1681\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-ap-chem\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EThe AP Chemistry Exam has 2 sections and lasts 3 hours and 15 minutes.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ESection I: Multiple Choice\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThe multiple-choice section has 60 questions and lasts 1 hour and 30 minutes. This section represents 50% of your total score. Your score on the multiple-choice section is based on the number of questions answered correctly. Points are not deducted for incorrect answers or unanswered questions.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ESection II: Free Response\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThe free-response section has 7 questions and lasts 1 hour and 45 minutes. This section represents 50% of your total score. Questions 1 through 3 are long free-response questions, each worth 10 points. Questions 4 through 7 are short free-response questions, each worth 4 points.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ETaking the Exam\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EEach section is timed separately. You can go back and forth between questions in a section until time expires. The clock will turn red when 5 minutes remain in the section\\u2014\\u003Cem\\u003Ethe proctor will not give you any time updates or warnings\\u003C\\/em\\u003E. You cannot move ahead to a different section. Once time expires in a section, you cannot return to it.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EA calculator and reference information, including a periodic table and lists of equations and constants, are available in this application and can be accessed throughout the exam.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EYou may use the available paper for scratch work, but credit for Section I: Multiple Choice will only be given for responses entered in this application. When time expires in a section, all answers you have already entered will be submitted.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EFor Section II: Free Response, the questions are in this application, but you must write your responses to the questions in the free-response booklet. Use a pencil or pen with black or dark blue ink. You may use the available paper for scratch work, but credit will only be given for responses that are written in the free-response booklet.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThere may be references in AP testing materials to companies, products, and brands that are owned by others and subject to trademark law. Neither College Board nor the AP testing materials are affiliated with or endorsed by these trademark owners.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222025-01-06T14:39:54-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1736192394\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1591\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-ap-phys-c-em-day2\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Day 2 Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EDay 2 of the AP Physics C: Electricity \\u0026amp; Magnetism Exam consists of the multiple-choice section.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003EMultiple Choice\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThe multiple-choice section has 40 questions and lasts 1 hour and 20 minutes. This section represents 50% of your total score. Your score on the multiple-choice section is based on the number of questions answered correctly. Points are not deducted for incorrect answers or unanswered questions.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ETaking the Exam\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EYou can go back and forth between questions in the section until time expires. The clock will turn red when 5 minutes remain\\u2014\\u003Cem\\u003Ethe proctor will not give you any time updates or warnings\\u003C\\/em\\u003E. Once time expires in the section, you cannot return to it.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EA calculator and reference information, including lists of equations, are available in this application and can be accessed throughout the exam.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EYou may use scratch paper for notes and planning, but credit will only be given for responses entered in this application. When time expires in the section, all answers you have already entered will be submitted.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThere may be references in AP testing materials to companies, products, and brands that are owned by others and subject to trademark law. Neither College Board nor the AP testing materials are affiliated with or endorsed by these trademark owners.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222025-01-06T14:38:14-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1736192294\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1631\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-ap-phys-c-em-day1\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Day 1 Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EDay 1 of the AP Physics C: Electricity \\u0026amp; Magnetism Exam consists of the free-response section.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003EFree Response\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThe free-response section has 4 questions and lasts 1 hour and 40 minutes. This section represents 50% of your total score. Questions 1 and 3 are worth 10 points each. Question 2 is worth 12 points. Question 4 is worth 8 points.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ETaking the Exam\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EYou can go back and forth between questions in the section until time expires. The clock will turn red when 5 minutes remain\\u2014\\u003Cem\\u003Ethe proctor will not give you any time updates or warnings\\u003C\\/em\\u003E. Once time expires in the section, you cannot return to it.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EA calculator and reference information, including lists of equations, are available in this application and can be accessed throughout the exam.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThe free-response questions are in this application, but you must write your responses to the questions in the free-response booklet. Use a pencil or pen with black or dark blue ink. You may use the available paper for scratch work, but credit will only be given for responses that are written in the free-response booklet.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThere may be references in AP testing materials to companies, products