e-response booklet. Use a pencil or pen with black or dark blue ink. You may use the available paper for scratch work, but credit will only be given for responses that are written in the free-response booklet.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThere may be references in AP testing materials to companies, products, and brands that are owned by others and subject to trademark law. Neither College Board nor the AP testing materials are affiliated with or endorsed by these trademark owners.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222025-01-06T14:40:34-05:00\\u0022\\u003E1736192434\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"1571\",\"internal_id\":\"checkin-overview-ap-comp-sci-a-day2\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Day 2 Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EDay 2 of the AP Computer Science A Exam consists of the multiple-choice section.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003EMultiple Choice\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThe multiple-choice section has 42 questions and lasts 1 hour and 30 minutes. This section represents 55% of your total score. Your score on the multiple-choice section is based on the number of questions answered correctly. Points are not deducted for incorrect answers or unanswered questions.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ETaking the Exam\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EYou can go back and forth between questions in the section until time expires. The clock will turn red when 5 minutes remain\\u2014\\u003Cem\\u003Ethe proctor will not give you any time updates or warnings\\u003C\\/em\\u003E. Once time expires in the section, you cannot return to it.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EJava Quick Reference information can be accessed in this application and is available throughout the exam.\