u003Cp\\u003EThere may be references in AP testing materials to companies, products, and brands that are owned by others and subject to trademark law. Neither College Board nor the AP testing materials are affiliated with or endorsed by these trademark owners.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\",\"id\":\"checkin-overview-ap-euro-hist-day1-p1\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-06-25T17:09:58-04:00\\u0022\\u003E1782421798\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"2671\",\"internal_id\":\"overview-ap-euro-hist-linear-singleday\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EThe AP European History Exam has 2 sections and lasts 3 hours and 15 minutes. Section I has 2 parts.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ESection I, Part A: Multiple Choice\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThe multiple-choice part has 55 questions and lasts 55 minutes. This part represents 40% of your total score. Your score on the multiple-choice part is based on the number of questions answered correctly. Points are not deducted for incorrect answers or unanswered questions.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ESection I, Part B: Short Answer\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThe short-answer part has 3 short-answer questions and lasts 40 minutes. This part represents 20% of your total score for the exam, and each of the 3 questions counts equally toward your score.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ESection II: Free Response\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThe free-response section has 1 document-based question (DBQ) and 1 long essay question and lasts 1 hour and 40 minutes. This section represents 40% of your total score for the exam. The DBQ represents 25% of your score on the exam, and the long essay question represents 15% of your score on the exam.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ETaking the Exam\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EEach section and part is timed separately. You can go back and forth between questions in a section or part until time expires. The clock will turn red when 5 minutes remain in the section or part\\u2014\\u003Cem\\u003Ethe proctor will not give you any time updates or warnings\\u003C\\/em\\u003E. You cannot move ahead to a different section or part. Once time expires in a section or part, you cannot return to it.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EYou may use scratch paper for notes and planning, but credit will only be given for responses entered in this application. Any text you enter as an annotation will \\u003Cem\\u003Enot\\u003C\\/em\\u003E be included in your answer submissions. When time expires in a section or part, all answers you have already entered will be submitted.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003ESource materials may have been edited for the purpose of this exam.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThe inclusion of source material in this exam is not intended as an endorsement by College Board of the content, ideas, or values expressed in the material. The sources that appear in the AP European History Exam represent a range of different authors, historical periods, and perspectives, as appropriate for measuring the college-level knowledge and skills that are the focus of this course. AP students are not expected or asked to subscribe to any specific cultural or political values, but they are expected to analyze perspectives that may be different from their own and to analyze and interpret sources in historical context.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThere may be references in AP testing materials to companies, products, and brands that are owned by others and subject to trademark law. Neither College Board nor the AP testing materials are affiliated with or endorsed by these trademark owners.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\"}],\"cancel_interaction\":[],\"confirm_interaction\":[],\"offering\":\"AP\",\"delivery_method\":\"\",\"changed\":\"\\u003Ctime datetime=\\u00222026-06-25T17:09:58-04:00\\u0022\\u003E1782421798\\u003C\\/time\\u003E\\n\"},{\"id\":\"2666\",\"internal_id\":\"overview-ap-us-hist-linear-multiday-part2\",\"type\":\"functional_content\",\"title\":\"Day 2 Exam Overview\",\"short_title\":\"\",\"alternate_title\":\"\",\"internal_description\":\"\",\"external_description\":\"\",\"overview\":\"\",\"content\":[{\"content\":\"\\u003Cp\\u003EDay 2 of the AP United States History Exam has 2 parts.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003EPart A: Multiple Choice\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThe multiple-choice part has 55 questions and lasts 55 minutes. This part represents 40% of your total score. Your score on the multiple-choice part is based on the number of questions answered correctly. Points are not deducted for incorrect answers or unanswered questions.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003EPart B: Short Answer\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EThe short-answer part has 3 short-answer questions and lasts 40 minutes. This part represents 20% of your total score for the exam, and each of the 3 questions counts equally toward your score.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Ch2\\u003ETaking the Exam\\u003C\\/h2\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EEach part is timed separately. You can go back and forth between questions in a part until time expires. The clock will turn red when 5 minutes remain in a part\\u2014\\u003Cem\\u003Ethe proctor will not give you any time updates or warnings\\u003C\\/em\\u003E. You cannot move ahead to a different part. Once time expires in a part, you cannot return to it.\\u003C\\/p\\u003E\\u003Cp\\u003EYou may use scratch paper for notes and planning, but credit will only be given for responses entered in this application. Any text you enter as an annotation will \\u003Cem\\u003Enot \\u003C\\/em\\u003Ebe included in your answer submissions. When time expires in a part, all answers you have already entered will be submitted.\\u003C\\/p\\